---
// ===========================================================================
// TypeAndInstance.astro — the two lanes, which is the whole page in one look.
//
// Readers reach for a prop or a context to carry the type, because that is how
// everything else works. The point is that the type takes a different road
// entirely: the instance travels at run time through React, and the type
// travels at compile time through the compilation. Drawing them as two lanes
// says it faster than the paragraphs it replaces.
// ===========================================================================
---

<figure class="mt-8">
  <!-- Scrolls rather than shrinks. Scaled to a 375px column the labels come
       out around five pixels tall, which is a diagram nobody can read; the
       minimum width keeps them legible and the page still never scrolls. -->
  <div class="overflow-x-auto">
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 720 300"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="lanes-title lanes-desc"
    class="w-full min-w-[620px]"
  >
    <title id="lanes-title">The instance and the type take different roads</title>
    <desc id="lanes-desc">
      One adapter feeds two lanes. At run time the form instance travels down
      the React tree through a provider and a component receives it by being
      inside one. At compile time the same adapter is registered by a module
      augmentation, which belongs to the whole compilation, so a component is
      type-checked without importing or receiving anything.
    </desc>

    <g
      font-family="var(--md-font-sans, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif)"
      fill="var(--md-on-surface)"
    >
      <!-- source -->
      <rect x="250" y="8" width="220" height="40" rx="8"
        fill="var(--md-primary-container)" />
      <text x="360" y="26" font-size="13" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle"
        fill="var(--md-on-primary-container)">zodFormResolver(orderSchema)</text>
      <text x="360" y="41" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle"
        fill="var(--md-on-primary-container)">one adapter</text>

      <path d="M 300 48 L 300 62 L 150 62 L 150 84" fill="none"
        stroke="var(--md-outline)" stroke-width="1.5" />
      <path d="M 420 48 L 420 62 L 570 62 L 570 84" fill="none"
        stroke="var(--md-outline)" stroke-width="1.5" />

      <!-- lane headings -->
      <text x="150" y="80" font-size="11" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle"
        fill="var(--md-on-surface-variant)">AT RUN TIME</text>
      <text x="570" y="80" font-size="11" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle"
        fill="var(--md-on-surface-variant)">AT COMPILE TIME</text>

      <!-- left lane: the instance -->
      <rect x="24" y="88" width="252" height="52" rx="8"
        fill="var(--md-surface-container-high)" stroke="var(--md-outline-variant)" />
      <text x="40" y="110" font-size="12.5" font-weight="600">createForm(adapter)</text>
      <text x="40" y="128" font-size="11" fill="var(--md-on-surface-variant)">the cell space — one per form on screen</text>

      <line x1="150" y1="140" x2="150" y2="162" stroke="var(--md-outline)" stroke-width="1.5" />

      <rect x="24" y="166" width="252" height="52" rx="8"
        fill="var(--md-surface-container-high)" stroke="var(--md-outline-variant)" />
      <text x="40" y="188" font-size="12.5" font-weight="600">&lt;FormProvider form={"{form}"}&gt;</text>
      <text x="40" y="206" font-size="11" fill="var(--md-on-surface-variant)">travels DOWN the React tree</text>

      <!-- right lane: the type -->
      <rect x="444" y="88" width="252" height="52" rx="8"
        fill="var(--md-surface-container-high)" stroke="var(--md-outline-variant)" />
      <text x="460" y="110" font-size="12.5" font-weight="600">declare module "@maroonedog/form-contract/react"</text>
      <text x="460" y="128" font-size="11" fill="var(--md-on-surface-variant)">FormTypeRegistry — one file, one time</text>

      <line x1="570" y1="140" x2="570" y2="162" stroke="var(--md-outline)" stroke-width="1.5" />

      <rect x="444" y="166" width="252" height="52" rx="8"
        fill="var(--md-secondary-container)" />
      <text x="460" y="188" font-size="12.5" font-weight="600"
        fill="var(--md-on-secondary-container)">the whole COMPILATION</text>
      <text x="460" y="206" font-size="11"
        fill="var(--md-on-secondary-container)">not the import graph — nothing is imported</text>

      <!-- they meet -->
      <path d="M 150 218 L 150 238 L 360 238 L 360 252" fill="none"
        stroke="var(--md-outline)" stroke-width="1.5" />
      <path d="M 570 218 L 570 238 L 360 238" fill="none"
        stroke="var(--md-outline)" stroke-width="1.5" />

      <rect x="196" y="252" width="328" height="40" rx="8"
        fill="var(--md-surface-container-high)" stroke="var(--md-outline-variant)" />
      <text x="360" y="270" font-size="13" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle"
        >useField("billing.postcode")</text>
      <text x="360" y="285" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle"
        fill="var(--md-on-surface-variant)">no import, no prop, and still checked</text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-on-surface-variant">
    The right-hand lane is the unusual one. A module augmentation belongs to the
    compilation, so a component ten levels down is checked by a file it has
    never heard of — and a registration that falls out of <code>tsconfig</code>'s{" "}
    <code>include</code> fails loudly rather than degrading back to{" "}
    <code>string</code>.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
